    "content": "As of March 13, 2026, the Kentucky State Police have issued an IAN Alert for a missing 9-year-old girl in Boone County. An IAN Alert is a Kentucky emergency system for missing children with autism or disabilities, which acts similarly to an Amber Alert. Key Details regarding IAN Alerts: Purpose: To quickly notify the public when a child with autism or a mental disability goes missing and may be in danger. Origin: Named after Ian Sousis, a 9-year-old with autism who drowned after wandering away, leading to a new Kentucky law in 2024. What to Do: If you receive an alert, check nearby bodies of water, pools, and surroundings, as children with autism are at higher risk of drowning. System: It utilizes the same wireless emergency alert system as Amber Alerts. Recent Alert: A previous IAN alert issued on March 11, 2026, in Lexington for a 17-year-old was canceled after he was found safe, according to LEX18 and WKYT. This information is based on reports from March 2026.",
